<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  WildAnimals_PoisonForest.xml               UtinniPatches — new file 2026-09-25
  ============================================================================

  Wires the campaign's Star Wars fauna onto RM_Cauldron's wildAnimals,
  layered on top of the 13 non-Star-Wars rows that mod ships inline (Genetic
  Rim/Alpha Animals/Alpha Memes/Horrors — Q9 permits those directly on a
  RM_ def). Per §7 Q11 ("RimMandrake should not name star wars ever"),
  RM_Cauldron may not carry any Star Wars creature by any route, so
  every one of the frozen RUT_Cauldron.xml's (renamed from RUT_PoisonForest,
  CAULDRON_FULL_RENAME_1, 2026-09-30) 5 Star Wars/campaign-tier
  rows rides HERE instead. Shape: WildAnimals_LeaningScrub.xml /
  WildAnimals_Pyrelands.xml.

  🔑 SOURCE OF TRUTH: every defName and weight below is copied verbatim from
  the LIVE RUT_Cauldron.xml wildAnimals block as of COMMISSION_LEDGER_
  CLEANUP_1's 2026-09-24/25 pass (18 rows total) — not from the stale
  POISONFOREST_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 item table (written 2026-09-23, before
  RSW_VentStalker was added).

  🔴 MLIE_ABSORPTION_BIOME_WIRING_1 (2026-09-25): the 3 rows once gated
  mlie.starwarsanimalcollection (Neebray, Mynock, GraniteSlug) all already
  have our own RSW_ ports too — retargeted into the single
  mandrake.rsw.swbestiary op below, alongside RSW_Screecher/RSW_VentStalker.
  CAULDRON_RULED_CONTENT_1 (2026-09-29) adds the owner-ruled imports: Lylek and
  Skalder (RSW_ ports, in the swbestiary op) and Silooth (donor row, its own
  FindMod op). Both ops now guard with PatchOperationFindMod; the old
  Operation MayRequire attribute was inert.

  RSW_Screecher is multi-homed on purpose (owner approved 2026-09-22,
  BIOME_SPECIFIC_FAUNA_LAW_1 — a real flier that migrates from this wetter
  biome into the hot Wasteland to lay; the law's own carve-out, not a
  violation. Do not "fix" it by cutting either home.

  No unconditional PatchOperationReplace op is needed here: RM_Cauldron's
  own BiomeDef already ships a real 13-species wildAnimals block inline, so
  both ops below are plain PatchOperationConditional + PatchOperationAdd
  onto that existing node.

  ⚠️ A patch that matches nothing logs nothing (PatchOperationConditional
  returns true on no match) — validated with
  skills/rimworld-modding/scripts/validate_patch.py against the live def
  dump and the full active mod set; an unmatched PatchOperationAdd is
  silent, so a clean run there is not proof a row landed.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- Our own RSW_ ports. Guard is PatchOperationFindMod on the mod NAME:
       an <Operation MayRequire=...> attribute is inert in the 1.6 engine. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>RimMandrake: SW — Bestiary</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationConditional">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Cauldron"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
        <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Cauldron"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
        <value>
          <RSW_Neebray>0.8</RSW_Neebray>
          <RSW_Mynock>0.2</RSW_Mynock>
          <RSW_GraniteSlug>0.15</RSW_GraniteSlug>
          <!-- MULTI-HOMED ON PURPOSE - see file header. -->
          <RSW_Screecher>0.35</RSW_Screecher>
          <RSW_VentStalker>0.25</RSW_VentStalker>
          <!-- CAULDRON_RULED_CONTENT_1: owner-ruled imports, wired and kept
               on purpose (overrides the frozen sheet's no-grazer line for
               Lylek and Skalder). Do not "fix" them back out. -->
          <RSW_Lylek>0.05</RSW_Lylek>
          <RSW_Skalder>0.08</RSW_Skalder>
        </value>
      </match>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- CAULDRON_RULED_CONTENT_1: Silooth is a donor row (Star Wars Animal
       Collection) with no RSW_ port; owner-ruled import, wired and kept. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Star Wars Animal Collection (Continued)</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationConditional">
      <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Cauldron"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
      <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
        <xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RM_Cauldron"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
        <value>
          <Silooth>0.5</Silooth>
        </value>
      </match>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
